  "id": "reproduction-theory",
  "term": "reproduction theory",
  "definition": "Reproduction theory describes the idea that investing resources in offspring now can limit resources available for later reproduction, creating a trade-off between present and future reproductive effort. In this packet, it is discussed alongside age-related strategies in which individuals may either increase or reduce current investment to improve overall lifetime reproductive success.",
